Git glyphs

The seven files here are GitHub's Octicons at their 16 px size, unmodified, from
primer/octicons (icons/*-16.svg, retrieved 2026-10-06). Octicons are MIT licensed, copyright
GitHub Inc.; see LICENSE-octicons.

They draw the chrome's git vocabulary (a branch, a pull request open, draft or closed, a
merge, a commit, a repository), which SF Symbols lacks. Each is filled from its outline into
an alpha mask and painted in the ink of the words beside it, as an SF Symbol is.
